+# 0002 — Member account and borrowing block
+
+## Context
+
+Fines, manual staff charges and payments need somewhere to live, and members
+who owe too much must stop borrowing. The owner settled these rules on 2026-10-28.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Each member has a single **balance**. Overdue fines, manual charges and every
+  future fee (e.g. the no-show fee, ADR 0003) go on it, and all of them count
+  toward every block.
+- The account is a ledger of entries (fine / charge / payment) in the
+  repository. The balance is always derived from the entries and never stored
+  separately.
+- **No credit.** A payment above the balance is refused with `InvalidAmount`, so
+  the balance never goes negative.
+- Amounts accepted by `pay` and `add_charge` must be a `Decimal`, finite,
+  positive, and in whole cents. Anything else raises `InvalidAmount`. A manual
+  charge also needs a non-blank reason.
+- A refused operation changes nothing.
+- **Borrowing block:** a balance ≥ 10.00 (`policy.BORROW_BLOCK_AT`) makes
+  `checkout` raise `AccountBlocked`. The same bar applies to adults and children.
+- Returning copies and paying **always** work, even while the member is blocked.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Adding a refund or waiver later means adding a new entry kind, and deciding
+  whether credit becomes allowed. That decision would reverse "no credit".
+- Each new block (for example the hold bar in ADR 0003) is another threshold
+  compared against the same balance.
