+# 0004 — Renewals charge lateness accrued so far (planned)
+
+Status: accepted; built with renewals. Stated by the owner on 2026-10-28. The
+open cap question is settled by ADR 0007: the cap applies per loan.
+
+## Context
+
+Fines are charged on return (ADR 0001). If renewing an overdue loan moved its
+due date forward, the lateness before the renewal would vanish.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Renewing a loan that is already overdue **charges the late fine built up so
+  far as part of the renewal**. It is counted exactly as if the copy had been
+  returned on the renewal day, with the usual rates, cap and child exemption
+  (`policy.late_fine` with the renewal day as the "as of" day).
+- After the renewal, lateness is counted against the new due date.
+- Lateness before a renewal must never just disappear. Tests for renewals must
+  prove it.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A loan can end up with more than one fine entry: one per overdue renewal,
+  plus one at return.
+- Still open: whether the replacement-cost cap applies per charge or to the
+  total over the whole loan. As written ("as if returned on the renewal day"),
+  each charge is capped separately, so a loan renewed several times could add
+  up to more than the replacement cost in total. Confirm this with the owner
+  before building renewals.
