+# 0005 — Hold queue, pickup time and expiry
+
+## Context
+
+ADR 0003 fixed the hold bar and the no-show fee but left two questions open:
+how long the pickup time is, and what triggers the fee. The owner settled these,
+along with how the queue behaves, on 2026-10-28.
+
+## Decision
+
+- A member can place a hold only when **no copy of the title is AVAILABLE** and
+  at least one copy is in circulation (not withdrawn). They cannot hold a title
+  they already have an active hold on, or one they currently have a copy of on
+  loan. These refusals raise `HoldNotAllowed`. The 5.00 balance bar (ADR 0003)
+  raises `AccountBlocked`.
+- The queue is **first come, first served** by placement order.
+- A copy comes to the hold shelf only on **return** (or when it is passed on,
+  see below). A returned copy goes to the first WAITING hold (READY). Copies
+  added with `add_copy` go on the open shelf and do not serve the queue.
+- **Pickup time:** `pickup_by` = the day the copy is set aside + 7 calendar
+  days. If that is a Sunday (closed), it becomes the next Monday. `pickup_by` is
+  the last day to collect, and a hold expires only once `pickup_by` is before
+  today (`policy.pickup_by`, `policy.PICKUP_DAYS`).
+- **Trigger:** a daily job, `expire_holds`, expires overdue READY holds and
+  charges the no-show fee (adults only). The fee is its own ledger entry kind,
+  `EntryKind.NO_SHOW_FEE`.
+- When a READY hold expires or is cancelled, its copy is **passed on** to the
+  next WAITING hold, with `pickup_by` counted from the day that happens. If
+  nobody is waiting, the copy goes back on the shelf. A job that missed days
+  counts from the day it actually runs.
+- WAITING holds never expire. Cancelling costs nothing.
+- Only the member whose READY hold a copy is set aside for can borrow it. Normal
+  loan-limit and borrowing-block checks still apply.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `pickup_by` is fixed when the copy is set aside, but the expiry happens only
+  when the job runs. If the job is late, a member can still collect after
+  `pickup_by` until it runs.
+- New copies bypass the queue, so a member with a WAITING hold may borrow a new
+  copy and still hold their place. Revisit this if it causes trouble at the desk.
+- Renewals (ADR 0004, ADR 0006) read the queue: WAITING holds block renewing the
+  title.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0006-renewal-eligibility.md b/docs/adr/0006-renewal-eligibility.md
