@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# 0006 — Who may renew (planned)
+
+Status: accepted; built with renewals. Stated by the owner on 2026-10-28. Read
+together with ADR 0004. The open questions are settled by ADR 0007.
+
+## Context
+
+Renewing a loan keeps a copy away from everyone else. That shouldn't happen
+while other members are queuing for the title, or while the borrower owes the
+library money.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Queue block:** a loan cannot be renewed while the title has any **WAITING**
+  hold. READY holds don't count, because that member already has a copy set
+  aside for them on the hold shelf.
+- **Paid-up only:** a member can renew only if their balance is zero when they
+  ask. Anything owed (fines, manual charges, no-show fees), even 0.01, blocks
+  renewal until it is paid. This bar is stricter than both the 5.00 hold bar and
+  the 10.00 borrowing bar.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The paid-up check uses the balance **before** the renewal. The accrued fine
+  that renewing an overdue loan charges (ADR 0004) doesn't count against the
+  same request. It will, however, block the *next* renewal until it is paid.
+- Still open: which error class each refusal raises (`AccountBlocked` fits the
+  balance bar; the queue block may need its own), and whether the 10.00
+  borrowing block also matters (it is implied by "paid up").
