+# 0007 — Renewal limits, window, errors, and the per-loan fine cap
+
+Status: accepted; built with renewals. Stated by the owner on 2026-10-28.
+Settles the questions left open in ADR 0004 and ADR 0006.
+
+## Context
+
+ADRs 0004 and 0006 fixed the accrued fine on overdue renewals, the queue block
+and the paid-up rule. Still open were: what can be renewed and how often, when,
+how the new due date is counted, which error each refusal raises, and whether
+the replacement-cost cap applies per charge or per loan.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Books only.** DVD loans are never renewable.
+- **At most 2 renewals per loan** (`policy.MAX_RENEWALS`).
+- **Window:** a loan can be renewed from 5 days before its *current* due date
+  onwards (`policy.RENEW_WINDOW_DAYS`). There is no upper limit, so overdue loans
+  can be renewed (and pay their accrued fine, ADR 0004).
+- **New due date** = the renewal day + the loan period, as for a checkout made
+  that day (`policy.due_date`), with Sunday → Monday.
+- **Errors:** an unknown loan raises `LoanNotFound`. A balance above zero raises
+  `AccountBlocked`. Every other refusal (returned loan, DVD, outside the window,
+  limit reached, WAITING hold on the title) raises `RenewalRefused`.
+- **Fine cap per loan:** the replacement-cost cap applies to the **total** of the
+  overdue fines charged for one loan: each overdue renewal plus the return. Each
+  charge is capped at what is left of the replacement cost after the earlier
+  fines on that loan. This replaces the per-charge reading in ADR 0004.
+- The paid-up bar (ADR 0006) applies to children as well, the same as every other
+  balance bar (ADR 0002). Children are still never fined (ADR 0001).
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Fine entries must carry their `loan_id`, so that the fines already charged on a
+  loan can be added up. Every overdue fine entry already does.
+- Lateness can never cost a member more than replacing the copy, however often
+  the loan is renewed.
+- A renewal count is stored on the loan. There is no per-renewal log, so earlier
+  due dates are not kept.
+- Allowing DVD renewals or changing the limit later means changing `policy`
+  only. Loans already renewed keep their count.
